`--project` moves marker resolution to the named root: the pinned vault records a current watermark
and renders, even though cwd's own marker is behind and would gate this playbook without the flag.
The second invocation is the same playbook from the same cwd with the flag dropped.

Discovery is pinned along with the marker, so the fixture playbook lives in the pinned vault's
`_playbooks` root.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
-- fixtures/cwd/pinned/.booping --
project_name: pinned
latest_migration: 999
-- fixtures/cwd/pinned/_playbooks/fx-pinned/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-pinned
title: Pinned
summary: Renders only when the marker comes from the pinned root.
---

Preamble from the pinned vault.
-- fixtures/cwd/pinned/_playbooks/fx-pinned/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  only: []
-- fixtures/cwd/pinned/_playbooks/fx-pinned/only/prompt.md --
---
name: only
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-pinned --project pinned
booping render-playbook fx-pinned
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Preamble from the pinned vault.

